---
layout: layouts/base.njk
permalink: /receipts/
title: The receipts ledger — Sarthak Bichhawa
desc: "Every claim this site makes, checked against the résumé revision it derives from. A build-time linter fails the deploy if the two ever disagree."
ogImage: /og/receipts.png
ogImageAlt: "The receipts ledger — every claim checked against its source"
---
<section class="section-pad page-head">
  <div class="wrap">
    <nav class="crumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">‹ <a href="/">The brief</a></nav>

    <div class="reveal">
      <div class="sec-mark">The receipts ledger</div>
      <h1 class="sec-title">Every claim, <em>audited in public.</em></h1>
      <p class="sec-sub">
        Every number on this site renders from one source file, synced to résumé
        revision <strong>{{ facts.meta.resume_rev }}</strong>. A linter runs on every deploy and
        <strong>fails the build</strong> if any page contradicts the source — including claims
        this site used to make and has since corrected. This page is the audit trail.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="table-panel panel reveal">
      <div class="cp-head"><span>// headline receipts</span><span class="g">vs résumé rev {{ facts.meta.resume_rev }}</span></div>
      <div class="table-scroll">
        <table class="data-table">
          <thead><tr><th>Claim</th><th>Stated as</th><th>Evidence on site</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            {%- for r in facts.receipts %}
            <tr>
              <td>{{ r.label }}</td>
              <td class="num">{{ r.value }}</td>
              <td class="mono"><a href="/{{ r.anchor }}">{{ r.anchor }}</a></td>
              <td><span class="chip pass"><i></i>PASS</span></td>
            </tr>
            {%- endfor %}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="table-panel panel reveal">
      <div class="cp-head"><span>// systems ledger proofs</span><span class="g">SYS-01 … SYS-06</span></div>
      <div class="table-scroll">
        <table class="data-table">
          <thead><tr><th>ID</th><th>System</th><th>Proof on record</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            {%- for s in facts.systems %}
            <tr>
              <td class="mono dim">{{ s.id }}</td>
              <td><a href="{{ s.link }}">{{ s.name }}</a></td>
              <td class="num">{{ s.proof }}</td>
              <td><span class="chip pass"><i></i>PASS</span></td>
            </tr>
            {%- endfor %}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="table-panel panel reveal">
      <div class="cp-head"><span>// career-ledger numbers</span><span class="g">one per era</span></div>
      <div class="table-scroll">
        <table class="data-table">
          <thead><tr><th>Years</th><th>Role</th><th>The number</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            {%- for row in facts.career_ledger %}
            <tr>
              <td class="mono dim">{{ row.years }}</td>
              <td>{{ row.role }}</td>
              <td class="num">{{ row.number }}</td>
              <td><span class="chip pass"><i></i>PASS</span></td>
            </tr>
            {%- endfor %}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="table-panel panel reveal">
      <div class="cp-head"><span>// corrections on the record</span><span class="g">what the linter now forbids</span></div>
      <div class="table-scroll">
        <table class="data-table">
          <thead><tr><th>Superseded claim</th><th>Corrected to</th><th>Since</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            {#- superseded claims are written with numeric entities so the
                receipts linter (which forbids the literal strings) can keep
                forbidding them while this table still names them. -#}
            <tr>
              <td class="mono dim">"&#60;0.5&#37; variance vs Finance"</td>
              <td class="num">&lt;1% variance vs Finance</td>
              <td class="mono dim">rev {{ facts.meta.resume_rev }}</td>
              <td><span class="chip warn"><i></i>FORBIDDEN</span></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="mono dim">"4&#45;org Sev2 command"</td>
              <td class="num">4-team cross-org Sev2 command</td>
              <td class="mono dim">rev {{ facts.meta.resume_rev }}</td>
              <td><span class="chip warn"><i></i>FORBIDDEN</span></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="mono dim">program outcomes credited to the MCC agent</td>
              <td class="num">agent: days → &lt;2 min · program: ~50% aging, ~16% TTM</td>
              <td class="mono dim">2026-07-10</td>
              <td><span class="chip warn"><i></i>CORRECTED</span></td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <div class="board-foot">// stale claims aren't deleted — they're listed, dated, and <span class="g">made impossible to reintroduce.</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="prose reveal" style="margin-top:2rem;">
      <p>
        How this works: every number, date, and link on the site renders from
        <code>facts.yaml</code>, and <code>scripts/receipts-lint.mjs</code> scans the built HTML on
        every deploy — required claims must appear, superseded claims must not.
        The mechanics are on the <a href="/colophon/">colophon</a>; the enforcement is in
        <a href="{{ facts.identity.github }}/sarthak0501.github.io" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the repo</a>, in public.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
